Where to change version numbers

Always do a complete rebuild after changing the version number.

The standard Apple version number must be used, and the correct "d", "a"
and "b" levels comformed to. See Apple IIgs technote #100 "Versionville"
for more details.

Init and CDEV *MUST* be changed together.

Init:
- BUILD.EQU.S 
Label "VERASC" ASC pseudo op; change text of version number
- I.RES 
 rVersion resource ($1); change version number and copyright year

* Note: Label VERSION is the master version number for tools, and should
  always be 3.0. $8000 changed to $0000 once no longer development version.

CDev:
- C.RES
   rTextForLETextBox2 resource ($1000); maintain the copyright year
- C.RES
   rCDEVFlags resource ($1); change version number and copyright year

Link layers:
- xxx.CODE.S
   xxxVERSH and xxxVERSL labels; change version number
- xxx.RES 
   rVersion resource ($1); change version number and copyright year
- xxx.CONFIG.S 
   EGGALERT; maintain the copyright year

Tool054:
Tool054 reads the version number from the Init. Therefore it does not
need to be changed or rebuilt.

Casper:
- Casper.S
   Many locations within the source file
- Casper.Res
   rVersion resource ($1); change version number and copyright year

Telnet:
- Telnet.S
   One location within the source file
